Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Current Build Host Pilot P0 Threat Review

@ [threat_review_uuid] 6a29b8a4-c6be-407b-a3e1-d3141a8c4bc5

& [Threats]
  + wrong-host or stale-commit deployment package substitution path traversal case-fold collision reparse escape final-root overwrite partial transfer unlisted executable digest laundering output spoof protected-root drift provider restart orphan process and performance overclaim
  + historical fixture content could resolve reads outside the pilot root or cause provider/network effects if admitted without dependency closure
  + permissive inherited ACL could allow later byte replacement even after a successful observation

& [Controls]
  + exact host/ref/commit/root constants closed manifest grammar bounded membership local and remote SHA256 unique staging atomic directory rename no-overwrite pre/post conservation process/listener audits independent output verification and typed fail-closed optional query
  + do not invoke arbitrary strings shells scripts URLs environment-derived commands or remote paths from manifest values; command vectors are fixed by reviewed implementation

& [ResidualRisk]
  + SSH transport and Windows host administration are trusted operational dependencies; SHA256 binds bytes but does not sign publisher identity or prove the host remained uncompromised
  + P0 reports ACL posture and portability only and withholds production-trust autonomy and semantic-performance claims
